        <span class="section-tag">Local Case Scenario</span>
        <h2>Real-World Solution: Upgrading a Freezing Propane Water Heater in a Grant Country Home</h2>
        <p>
          A homeowner on North 3500 East experienced freezing water lines and repeated pilot failure on their water heater located in an attached unheated utility room during a -15°F cold snap. Our technician insulated the incoming and outgoing water lines with self-regulating heat tape, cleaned the propane pilot burner assembly, and installed an insulated thermal jacket. We also adjusted the gas pressure to factory specs, ensuring reliable hot water through the remainder of the winter.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Transparent Estimates Section -->
